# 3m_Mile_Server
================================================================
3mMile Backend API — README
================================================================

OVERVIEW
--------
Node.js + Express + MongoDB (Mongoose) backend API.
Uses JWT authentication, role/permission-based authorization,
Zod validation, Winston logging, and Docker for local/dev/prod
environments. Nginx sits in front of the API as a reverse proxy.

TECH STACK
----------
- Runtime:      Node.js 22 (Alpine, via Docker)
- Framework:    Express 5
- Database:     MongoDB 7 + Mongoose
- Cache/Queue:  Redis 8 (configured, not yet wired into business logic)
- Auth:         JSON Web Tokens (access + refresh)
- Validation:   Zod
- Logging:      Winston (+ daily rotate file in production)
- Security:     Helmet, CORS, express-rate-limit
- Reverse proxy: Nginx (Alpine)
- Containerization: Docker + docker-compose (base / dev / prod overlays)

----------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT STRUCTURE
----------------------------------------------------------------
src/
  App/app.js              -> Express app setup (middleware, routes mount)
  server.js                -> Entry point: connects DB, starts server, handles shutdown
  DB/
    connection/             -> Mongoose connection logic
    models/                 -> Mongoose schemas (User, Role, Product, Category,
                               Service, Branch, Booking, BlogPost, AuditLog, ...)
  routes/                   -> Express routers, one file per resource
  controllers/              -> Request handlers (thin, call services)
  services/                 -> Business logic + DB access (crud.service.js is
                               a generic reusable CRUD layer over any model)
  middleware/                -> auth, permission, validation, rate limiting,
                               file upload, global error handling
  validators/                -> Zod schemas per resource
  helpers/                   -> query building, DB aggregation helpers
  utils/                      -> JWT, logger, response formatter, security, etc.
  constants/                  -> Central app-wide constants/config

scripts/
  seed.js                    -> Creates base Admin role + initial admin user

nginx/                        -> Reverse proxy config + SSL placeholder
Dockerfile                    -> Multi-stage build (development / production)
start.sh                      -> Container entrypoint (runs seed if enabled,
                               then starts the server in the right mode)
docker-compose.yaml            -> Base service definitions
docker-compose.dev.yaml        -> Local development overrides
docker-compose.prod.yaml       -> Production overrides

----------------------------------------------------------------
ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (.env)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Create a `.env` file in the project root (never commit this file).
Required variables:

  NODE_ENV=development                # development | production | uat
  PORT=3000

  MONGODB_URI=mongodb://<user>:<pass>@mongo:27017/3mmile?authSource=admin
  MONGO_USERNAME=your_mongo_root_user
  MONGO_PASSWORD=your_mongo_root_password

  REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

  ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=change_this_to_a_long_random_secret
  REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=change_this_to_a_different_long_random_secret
  TOKEN_PREFIX=Bearer

  API_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8082      # used to build uploaded-file URLs
  CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000

  API_SERVER_NAME=localhost                 # used by nginx template
  API_UPSTREAM_HOST=3mMile-app               # used by nginx template

  RUN_DB_SEED=true                           # set true only for dev/staging
  SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
  SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=ChangeMe123!

  MONGO_EXPRESS_USERNAME=admin               # only needed if using dev-tools profile
  MONGO_EXPRESS_PASSWORD=admin

----------------------------------------------------------------
RUNNING LOCALLY (WITHOUT DOCKER)
----------------------------------------------------------------
1. Install dependencies:
     npm install

2. Make sure MongoDB and Redis are running locally (or point
   MONGODB_URI / REDIS_URL at remote instances).

3. (Optional) Seed initial data:
     node scripts/seed.js

4. Start in dev mode (auto-restart on file changes):
     npm run dev

5. Start in production mode:
     npm start

The API will be available at:  http://localhost:3000/api/v1
Health check:                   http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health

----------------------------------------------------------------
RUNNING WITH DOCKER (RECOMMENDED)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Development (hot-reload, exposed dev ports):

    docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml -f docker-compose.dev.yaml up --build

  - API (via nginx):     http://localhost:8082
  - API (direct, dev):   http://localhost:3001
  - Mongo Express (UI):  http://localhost:8081   (only if --profile dev-tools)
  - MongoDB exposed on:  localhost:27018
  - Redis exposed on:    localhost:6380

Production:

    docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml -f docker-compose.prod.yaml up --build -d

  - API (via nginx only): http://<server-ip>  (port 80)
  - MongoDB/Redis are NOT exposed to the host in production.

To stop:
    docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml -f docker-compose.dev.yaml down

----------------------------------------------------------------
SEEDING THE DATABASE
----------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/seed.js creates:
  - An "Admin" role with a starter set of permissions
  - One admin user (email/password from SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL /
    SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD env vars, or a random generated password
    printed once to the console if not set)

The script is idempotent — running it multiple times will not
create duplicates.

Run manually:
    node scripts/seed.js

Run inside a running container:
    docker compose exec 3mMile-app node scripts/seed.js

Automatic run on container start:
    Set RUN_DB_SEED=true in your .env — start.sh will run the seed
    automatically before starting the server. Recommended for local/
    dev/staging ONLY. Never enable this in production; run the seed
    manually, once, with real admin credentials instead.

----------------------------------------------------------------
API DOCUMENTATION
----------------------------------------------------------------
See postman.json in the project root — import it directly into
Postman (File > Import) to get a ready-made collection of every
current endpoint, with example request bodies and a {{baseUrl}}
variable you can point at local/dev/staging/prod.

----------------------------------------------------------------
AVAILABLE NPM SCRIPTS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  npm start        Start the server (production mode)
  npm run dev       Start the server with nodemon (auto-restart on changes)
  npm test          (placeholder — wire up Jest before relying on this)

----------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES / KNOWN GAPS (see full audit report for details)
----------------------------------------------------------------
- Product/Category/Service/Branch/Booking/BlogPost CRUD endpoints
  are not implemented yet — only Auth and Audit routes exist so far.
- No Order/Cart/Review/Coupon models yet.
- Redis is configured in docker-compose but not yet used by the app.
- Automated tests are not set up yet (npm test is a placeholder).
